# Copy to keystore.properties, which is untracked and refused by scripts/check-secrets.sh if it
# is ever tracked. See docs/deployment/signing.md before filling anything in.
#
# RELEASES ARE SIGNED ONLY IN CI (DEC-0104). .github/workflows/release.yml writes this file on the
# runner, with the keystore decoded into $RUNNER_TEMP, and the release key is never copied to a
# development machine. For a headset, build debug (./gradlew :app:assembleDebug). Any build signed
# through this file anywhere but the `release` environment is a debug build: never published.
#
# THE TWO PASSWORDS DO NOT GO IN THIS FILE (DEC-0049). The build reads them from the environment,
# FABRICVR_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD and FABRICVR_KEY_PASSWORD, which CI fills from its secrets. The build
# reads the file first and the environment second, so a plain file with the passwords in it still
# works — it is simply not the path, and this file is the one most likely to be opened,
# screenshotted or pasted while debugging a signing error.
#
# storeFile is an ABSOLUTE path, OUTSIDE this repository. The previous version of this file said
# "paths are relative to the repository root" and suggested `release.keystore`, which put the
# project's one unrecoverable secret in a directory .gitignore did not cover (DEC-0049).
#
# There is no recovery if this key is lost: a signed build on a headset can only be upgraded by
# the same key, and the alternative is an uninstall that takes the notes, the vault and the
# 190 MB model with it.

storeFile=/absolute/path/outside/this/repo/fabric-vr-release.keystore
keyAlias=fabricvr

# Deliberately absent: storePassword, keyPassword.
